  "meta": {
    "title": "CGL Football",
    "show": "football",
    "version": "Take 2 (voices not yet swapped)",
    "fps": 24,
    "width": 1280,
    "height": 720,
    "notes": "The come-from-behind win. The booth bookends it; the middle is the game, with the announcers' voices over the plays. Every line is an on-camera booth generation by its speaker (one speaker, one sentence or one turn per take, started from a frame of Take 1's booth shot), laid as a line carrying its own stretch of that take; the booth shots show those same takes in step, Moose alone as a crop of the two-shot. The voice-over lines are the booth takes' own audio with the plays cut over it. The voices are the video model's own and not yet swapped to Eric and Roger (ElevenLabs had no credits): see the football-take2-swapped variant and fb2/swap-and-render.sh. Our graphics in Take 1's style: the bumper, the KEYS card (each key on Moose's first word), the score strips 3RD 14-13, 4TH 14-20, 4TH 0:41 14-20, 20-20 and 21-20, and the FINAL 21-20 box. Take 1's crowd bed, roars and gun, theme and sting, and its early-80s tape look."
  },
